15 0 obj
<< /A 34 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating blockchain technology's role in maritime applications. It shows how users, data, and technology layers using distributed ledger technology, consensus mechanisms, and smart contracts facilitate data exchange in port management, crew management, maritime insurance, environmental protection, and supply chain management. Companies like TradeLens and CargoX are involved, with challenges in technical, legal, regulatory, and industry acceptance areas.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 24 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 35 0 R /Alt (Flowchart showing data exchange between entities in shipping. Shippers, bank, customs, agent, and consignees are connected via data blocks and chain links. Linked below are shipping companies and port, involving documents and transport logistics.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
